xxHash

core/src/hash.c is an independent implementation of the one shot, unseeded,
default secret subset of the XXH3 64 bit algorithm. It embeds XXH3's 192 byte
default secret constant, which is reproduced from the reference implementation
because bit exact agreement with stock xxHash is a functional requirement: the
digest protocol has a server side computing row hashes, and a hash that were
merely "close" would silently produce wrong diffs rather than failing.

core/tests/xxh3_vectors.h holds expected hash values produced by running the
reference implementation's xxhsum, which the C tests then reproduce.

